A haiku summing up my feels on Empire:
Ahh, Enlightenment;
Empires, colonies, trade;
But no bug testing.
(As a German major who's all about Enlightenment-era Europe, I was also all about a grand strategy game that highlighted this period of history. However, with how buggy and broken this game was on release (and how even now, getting regiments across bridges is enough to want to rip your hair out), any grandness Empire: TW could've had was then crushed by Napoleon then after, which was a lot better polished and optimized. Though it's nice CA learned from their mistakes by Napoleon's release, but a shame Empire had to be a casualty to it in the meantime. I still recommend this game, however, as its low cost and third-party mods make the experience a bit more bearable.)

Abselutly stunning graphics, music, and overall atmosphere. You have very little control which Is boiled down to collecting coins and then "adding" a specific amount of coins to activate something and i really enjoy that for the most part;
Sometimes tho you end up wasting a lot of resources because you bought some knights or whatever and they are now standing with 4 of your archers each on the wrong side of your kingdom doing nothing while the other side is getting slaughtered - or builders constantly running to their death because they are fixated on chopping down trees / building something too far away / too late - or a whole town filled with guys standing around with a sythes because It's winter and they can't farm anymore, instead of just picking up a new tool.
Overall It's pretty great and defently worth your time - not sure about the 15 Euro price tag but if you spot it on sale go for it!

Shiny combo-breaker fast-action game with tons of cool guys and ladies (and no role).
Pros:
+ same old DMC character build: gather orbs and purchase combos and abilities. Allows you to build a character;
+ inspired settings, even if exploration can be boring;
+ learn well, play well: the game awards you for being fast, perceptive and cunning.
Cons:
- additional challenges are... too much challenging: a sub-average player can't win;
- some weapons' DPS is ridicolously higher than others' - I don't feel free to choose if the alternatives are "average" and "powerful";
- if you're too powerful, battles will end before the "S+" ratings are unlocked: you are undergraded because you're too "good".
All in all, a must have for combo-breakers or "relaxing" pure gameplay.

