Being pretty different from the original
,
is still a decent game. Compared to the first game and the Arma series, it is friendlier and is a great game for people not familiar with "realistic" shooters, because it nicely displays modern combat, better than most military shooters nowadays. The game's world is a single location, a big island, and unlike similar games there's no draw distance limit. Despite this the graphics are nice and well-optimized (for 2009). The story is nothing special and is pretty short, but the missions are fun. You drive vehicles, command your squad, use different firearms modeled after the real ones; a level editor is also included, as in the game's predecessor. The game's development probably was pushed by the publisher, so it can feel unpolished, there's cut content (some of it can still be found in the game's files), some annoying bugs, and not so good AI. I recommend
if you want a game that balances between "Hollywood action" (à la
